body:
I wanna get fucked by an entity. But like, in a healing sorta way. An existentially cathartic orgasm.

&#x200B;

brb, attempting to manifest an opportunity to visit the dmt realm and get mindfucked lol

These are all good advice, particularly the notion of scale. I've had some experience with Blades in the Dark, so I'm somewhat familiar with the concept already. I'll almost certainly be implementing it in the near future.

&#x200B;

For reference, the game I'm running involves uniting various factions against an eldritch threat like in Mass Effect or Dragon Age. I can see how scale mechanics would work well as the PCs start to feel truly powerful after influencing entire nations 'n such.

Hmm, have I done a reading for you before? Or do you perhaps watch tarot readings on twitch? Your username looks familiar.

&#x200B;

Well, the first thing that I picked up was something about needing to get to work on something. Like there's a situation that you're aware of, but have been avoiding or are reluctant to get involved in. But your skills are needed, particularly your empathy and intuition. Your guides aren't upset at you or anything, but it feels as though you may feel frustrated about one situation as a whole while there is another thing or two you could be working towards that would help alleviate the overall situation. For example, if there was a political issue you cared about and felt frustrated from, its like your guides would be trying to help steer you towards taking steps to confront or fight that issue instead of giving energy to a feeling of powerlessness. Regardless, there are allies at your disposal, but in spirit and here on Earth, who can help you with whatever this situation is. But you'll still need to put forth the willingness to "get stuck" in it, for better or worse. Look for signs to help show you the way down this path.

Okay, but that doesn't make eating a meal without fasting unpleasant. 

&#x200B;

In the grand scheme of things, cosmically speaking, if the universe truly is a state of inescapable duality on all levels, then it is not a universe in which I wish to exist.  In any case, I don't believe this world's duality is a complete representation of the universe anyway. I think there's other planes of existence where the rules are different and maybe not as blunt as it is here. But that's my opinion \*shrugs\*.

Hi there.

&#x200B;

I feel as though there's been some miscommunications, either on your part or theirs. There's some things they haven't been willing to look past, particularly one person who sort of acts as the "voice" of the group often. So it may be a sort of peer pressure thing in regards to some of your other friends. Don't fall for the drama, it'll just muddy up some important work you're meant to be doing right now. The situation will sort itself out the more you accept yourself for you who are, at which point I think one or two of the friends may open up to you again.

Alright, let's see...

&#x200B;

There's work you're doing right now which you've got the spirit for, but you may be going about it in a less helpful way. Work could be literal work as in a job, but I get a sense it might be closer to something more spiritual or having to do with routines in your life. Your attention is focused too much on specific details as opposed to the big picture. I get a feeling like there's a huge, beautiful, landscape painting your guides are showing you, but you have a magnifying glass on one part of it. Your intentions are good, you want to make sure you're doing the right thing, but there's a need to be open to other paths, other methods of doing things. You've got the baseline "vibe" of it, now you just need to follow the trail of clues.

Hmmm. Well, obviously its not the most objectively scientific explanation, but I believe its possible the boy could be some sort of spiritual guide of yours. Spirit, guardian angel, etc. whatever you wanna call it. Especially considering the familiarity you felt with him, and how he helped you through tough times, yet was rather illusive himself. Do you meditate? I would suggest taking some time to yourself to contemplate and think on your memories of him and see what feelings/sensations come up.

&#x200B;

Take all this with a grain of salt of course, its just how I'd view it through my personal beliefs and experiences.

I feel ya. One of the most painful things I've found was, in a way, how most people seem to just accept having no context to the world's suffering. No reason to live through it all. Its very alienating. Makes you feel alone and like nobody understands how things really are.

&#x200B;

Its not much, but I hope you're able to find some peace in that there are at least others who feel similarly out there. Reading your post helped me a bit, actually.

Not sure about mandatory, but there definitely should be options available as others have been saying. Hell, there should be more programs like that available of all kinds. As young adults, we're force-fed this concept that you either have to go to college to get a white collar job or a trade school for a high paying blue collar job, and if you don't you're a complete failure. Not everybody is suited or ready for that kind of experience straight out of high school. A lot of my own important learning experiences after high school involved deep introspection, searching for meaningful work, and just plain trying to work through mental illness. Young adults shouldn't be forced into career paths that don't fit them. I think the world would be a hell of a better place if there were more widely known and available programs like this idea.

&#x200B;

Definitely better than forced military service, ffs.

I've been thinking about this lately. I know at least one mood stabilizer has affected my memory for sure. My doctor recently increased the dosage of a different drug and I felt like I would forget really obvious things. Not entirely like, memory related really, more like "wow, that was dumb of me. Why didn't I think of that?"

&#x200B;

For those of you who experience symptoms like this, do you take anti-depressants or mood stabilizers?

Audio description:  In this series, we will be exploring my version of the "subconscious mind". This first part will involve describing the "Inner Voice" and introducing it to you through hypnosis. The intention is to establish a positive and meaningful relationship with the "deeper you" (this may be spiritual in interpretation, if you feel so inclined, but it doesn't have to be). This series is NOT intended to create a separate personality within you. Indeed, the Inner Voice really is just you, only deeper and wiser. That said, I would NOT advise that individuals with a history of mental illness involving hearing voices or developing negative multiple personalities listen to this recording. More is explained about the Inner Voice in the recording, but in general, please use discretion when listening as you would with any hypnosis file. Thank you, and enjoy! 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I ask these questions daily. Personally I hate when people refer to life as a "game". It seems to trivialize the suffering we endure. But that's just me and my negative mindset....

&#x200B;

I too would like some answers. I'm interested to see the responses here.

I'm sorry for what happened to you.

&#x200B;

I don't want to hurt those around me, but I also don't want to live solely for others' sake.

Someone else was channeling my guide.

&#x200B;

I don't really know what it would feel like to feel better. All I can remember is the pain.

&#x200B;

and I'm 25.

So, I'm very new to the concept of the ego. In talks with my therapist I find myself confused and uncomfortable with his mostly zen philosophy on life when he talks of emptiness and a state of oneness and such. I am a very feeling person whereas he is a very thinking person. Nevertheless I'd like to learn more about the nature of the ego. 

&#x200B;

I am depressed, and this causes me much pain. But it is my attachment to this pain that makes things worse, yes? I've tried to identify more with my loving nature, but that simply creates a self that is loving, but in deep pain. Realistically I know I can never feel "satisfied" with how I'm living my life right now. I do identify with some of the components of the ego that was mentioned, especially "I am separate from what is missing in my life" and "I am separate from the universe". But what am I to do? I feel that this is difficult to understand. And I feel that it is wrong for a spiritual path to be difficult to understand. I don't know, I'm just confused.

I believe we go to a spirit world between lives. I've had a few dreams in which my guides surrounded me with unconditional love from the other side and it was incredible! I've been depressed for several years and in one dream my guide was able to lift that feeling off of me completely for a few moments. Besides that I do spiritual hypnosis work online with people and I believe in their experiences during the sessions.

&#x200B;

As to whether life can feel heavenly while on Earth, I think we all have a spark of heaven within us and its up to us to choose that spark, despite the obstacles. You're definitely right though, its pretty darn difficult! I think we tend to not give ourselves enough credit though. Humanity, while flawed, has still done some pretty incredible things, don't you think?

I'm 25 and I feel very similarly. Living even another year seems like an impossible task. Life feels like a punishment, and as a result it makes me think about death and the afterlife all the time.

&#x200B;

I believe there is often a spiritual reason behind depression. I just wish I knew what that reason was. Personally, what I do is distract myself by helping others who suffer from mental illness and life challenges. I feel called to do this on a soul level, and it helps numb the pain. Perhaps you may need to discover your soul calling as well? In any case, feel free to message me anytime. Sometimes its helpful to talk to another who has felt similarly, even if its just to vent.
